<%# The "new comment" composer of a ticket: the button row and the collapsed form,
    one block for both timeline orders (position: :top | :bottom decides only the
    margin). The stable id is the Turbo Stream target of posts#create - after a saved
    comment the controller streams this partial FRESH, which closes the form and
    empties the editor (collapse#connect hides the content again; reveal-after-frame
    handles the already-loaded timeline frame).
    Locals: ticket, post (nil for a fresh form), position. %>
<%# max-w-[70ch]: the composer is running text like the comments it produces
    (user mockup 05.09.2026). %>
<div id="new-post-composer-<%= ticket.id %>"
 class="<%= position == :top ? 'mb-4' : 'mt-4' %> max-w-[70ch] hidden"
     data-controller="reveal-after-frame collapse"
     data-reveal-after-frame-frame-id-value="ticket-timeline-<%= ticket.id %>">
  <%# Collapsed state (T5): an input-look line instead of centered buttons.
      Clicking it expands the card below via the same collapse controller.
      No "@ erwaehnen" hint - this editor has no mention feature, and a hint
      would promise one. %>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2" data-collapse-target="button">
    <button type="button"
            data-action="collapse#toggle"
            class="flex flex-1 cursor-text items-center rounded-lg border border-cream-400 bg-surface-raised px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:border-cream-600">
      <%= t('views.organisations.posts.form.write_comment') %>
    </button>

  </div>

  <%# Form - shown when the buttons are hidden %>
  <div data-collapse-target="content" class="mt-4 w-full">
    <% local_post = defined?(post) ? post : nil %>
    <%= render 'organisations/posts/form', ticket: ticket, post: local_post %>
  </div>
</div>
